---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
---

<Layout title="Rachel - A Strategic Card Game">
  <main>
    <Hero />

    <section class="features">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>How It Works</h2>

        <div class="feature-grid">
          <div class="feature">
            <div class="feature-icon">🃏</div>
            <h3>Match Cards</h3>
            <p>Play cards that match the top card by suit or rank. Can't play? Draw from the deck.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="feature">
            <div class="feature-icon">⚡</div>
            <h3>Special Cards</h3>
            <p>2s force draws, 7s skip players, Black Jacks attack, Red Jacks defend, Queens reverse, Aces change suit.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="feature">
            <div class="feature-icon">🏆</div>
            <h3>Last One Loses</h3>
            <p>Empty your hand to get out. The last player holding cards loses the game.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="multiplayer">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Play Your Way</h2>
        <div class="modes">
          <div class="mode">
            <h3>Solo</h3>
            <p>Face the emissaries of the multiverse, at Easy, Medium, or Hard.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="mode">
            <h3>Local Multiplayer</h3>
            <p>Play with friends nearby using Game Center or local networking.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="mode">
            <h3>iPhone &amp; iPad</h3>
            <p>One universal app. On iPad the table opens into a full horseshoe.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="mode coming-soon">
            <h3>Online</h3>
            <p>Coming soon: play with anyone, anywhere.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="multiverse">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>The Multiverse</h2>
        <p class="multiverse-intro">Rachel isn't just an iOS game. It's being ported to every computing platform that ever existed.</p>
        <div class="platforms">
          <span>ZX Spectrum</span>
          <span>Commodore 64</span>
          <span>Amiga</span>
          <span>NES</span>
          <span>Game Boy</span>
          <span>Atari ST</span>
          <span>Apple II</span>
          <span>MS-DOS</span>
          <span>+25 more</span>
        </div>
        <p class="multiverse-note">Same rules. Same 64-byte protocol. A ZX Spectrum can play against an iPhone. This is the plan.</p>

        <h3 class="emissary-heading">Their emissaries got here first</h3>
        <p class="emissary-intro">You don't wait for the ports to meet the multiverse. Fourteen emissaries already sit at your table, and they don't all come from machines.</p>

        <img src="/images/emissary-table.png" alt="Three emissaries seated around the Rachel table on iPad, each with their universe's badge and colour" class="emissary-shot" />

        <div class="emissaries">
          <div class="emissary">
            <h4>Sid <span class="universe">C64-1982</span></h4>
            <p>From a universe of three-voice symphonies and 64 honest kilobytes. Smug about it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="emissary">
            <h4>Speccy <span class="universe">ZX-1984</span></h4>
            <p>From a universe of bedroom coders, rubber keys, and glorious clashing colour. Plays chaos.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="emissary">
            <h4>The Scribe <span class="universe">MAMLUK-1370</span></h4>
            <p>From the origin universe &mdash; the first Rachel, before the world knew it. Teaches while winning.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="multiverse-note">The rift runs through time as well as hardware: a medieval copyist, a Victorian gambler, a deco card sharp, a neon-lit ghost from 2077. Each plays differently, and each has something to say about how you're doing.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <div class="container">
        <nav>
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
          <a href="/terms">Terms</a>
          <a href="/support">Support</a>
        </nav>
        <p class="copyright">&copy; 2026 Steve Hill</p>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .container {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .hero {
    padding: 6rem 0 4rem;
    text-align: center;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-green) 0%, #0f1419 100%);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .tagline {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .screenshots {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    padding: 0 1rem;
  }

  /* Every part of the phone - padding, notch, corner radii - is derived
     from --frame-w, so the whole device scales as one piece. Set only
     --frame-w and --frame-h to resize it; never hardcode the parts, or the
     notch drifts out of proportion at other widths. */
  .device-frame {
    --frame-w: 180px;
    --frame-h: 370px;
    --pad: calc(var(--frame-w) * 0.055);
    position: relative;
    width: var(--frame-w);
    height: var(--frame-h);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    background: #1c1c1e;
    border-radius: calc(var(--frame-w) * 0.167);
    padding: var(--pad);
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 2px #3a3a3c,
      0 15px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
  }

  .device-frame:nth-child(2) {
    --frame-w: 200px;
    --frame-h: 410px;
  }

  .device-frame:hover {
    transform: translateY(-8px);
  }

  .device-notch {
    position: absolute;
    top: var(--pad);
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: calc(var(--frame-w) * 0.45);
    height: calc(var(--frame-w) * 0.12);
    background: #1c1c1e;
    border-radius: 0 0 calc(var(--frame-w) * 0.07) calc(var(--frame-w) * 0.07);
    z-index: 10;
  }

  .device-screen {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: calc(var(--frame-w) * 0.111);
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: top;
    background: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.875rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--color-text);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: opacity 0.2s;
  }

  .button:hover {
    text-decoration: none;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  .button.disabled {
    opacity: 0.7;
    cursor: default;
  }

  .apple-logo {
    width: 1.25rem;
    height: 1.25rem;
  }

  .features, .multiplayer {
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .features {
    background: var(--color-bg-light);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .feature {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .feature-icon {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .feature h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .feature p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .modes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .mode {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--color-bg-light);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
  }

  .mode h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .mode p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .mode.coming-soon {
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .multiverse {
    padding: 4rem 0;
    background: var(--color-bg-light);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .multiverse-intro {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .platforms {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .platforms span {
    padding: 0.375rem 0.75rem;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .multiverse-note {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .emissary-heading {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }

  .emissary-intro {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin: 0 auto 2rem;
  }

  .emissary-shot {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 46rem;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .emissaries {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .emissary {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
  }

  .emissary h4 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }

  .emissary .universe {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.125rem;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .emissary p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  footer {
    padding: 3rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
  }

  footer .container {
    text-align: center;
  }

  footer nav {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .copyright {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  /* Keep this block last. It overrides base rules of equal specificity, so
     source order is what makes it win - an earlier copy of this media query
     silently did nothing, which left the phone notches full-size on small
     screens while the frames around them shrank. */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .screenshots {
      gap: 0.75rem;
    }
    .device-frame {
      --frame-w: 100px;
      --frame-h: 205px;
    }
    .device-frame:nth-child(2) {
      --frame-w: 120px;
      --frame-h: 245px;
    }
  }
</style>
